<html>
<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},
<p>Thank you for getting in touch with the Qantas Customer Care team. I’m sorry to hear that we were unable to serve you a meal on board your recent flight QF{{{Case.Flight_Number__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If moved to an earlier flight, use:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Last minute flight change</strong><br />
<br />
When customers move to an earlier flight at the last minute, our caterers will always do their best to provide an additional meal to the aircraft prior to departure. However, it isn’t always possible in the short time frame.<br />
<br />
<strong><em>If upgraded use:-</em></strong><br />
<br />
<strong>Last minute upgrade</strong><br />
<br />
When customers upgrade to Business Class on departure, our caterers will always do their best to get a new meal to the aircraft prior to your departure, but it isn’t always possible in the short time frame.<br />
<br />
<br />
<strong><em>If moved by staff add:-</em></strong><br />
<br />
<strong>Last minute change by staff</strong><br />
<br />
In these instances, our staff will advise customers that the flight is ‘catering not assured’ prior to upgrading, so that they can decide if they’re happy to risk flying without a meal.<br />
<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If moved via kiosk add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Last minute change via check-in kiosk</strong><br />
<br />
If customers change flights via the check-in kiosk, we display information on the screen underneath the ‘Alternative flights’ options before customers confirm their selection.<br />
<br />
I understand your confusion if you missed this information and I’m sorry our crew didn’t handle this as well as we would have expected.<br />
<br />
<strong>We value your opinion</strong><br />
<br />
Customer feedback plays an important role in our continuous improvement process so that we can provide you with exceptional service from start to finish.<br />
<br />
I wanted to assure you that your feedback has been shared with the relevant team for future improvement.<br />
<br />
Thank you for taking the time to tell us about your experience and we look forward to welcoming you onboard again soon.</p>
</body>
</html>